From 7bad09f5b39ee14d1d6d0b65c151895c01672f06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oxjmo <oxjmo@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:00:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] OnePlus 6 (enchilada): boot chain, rootfs, clock fix,
 userland up

Phases 5-8 of the SDM845 port, all verified on the phone:

- enchilada device config and platform expert for the loader; the
  kernel reaches launchd and the whole iOS userland (backboardd,
  SpringBoard) runs on the phone.
- redwood_usb.c: the DWC3 gadget / CDC-ECM stand-in, boot-arg usb=N.
- IOFindBSDRoot rootfast=1: decide the root device from the memory-map
  RAMDisk without IOKit matching (a real device tree keeps drivers
  matching forever); nodisp=1 gates the display stand-in.
- The clock bug: Qualcomm's hypervisor remaps the arch timer PPIs
  (INTIDs 16-19, per the device tree) -- enable those and treat them
  as timer expiry alongside the standard PPI 27.
